course: dictionary
lesson: 1668
title: Choice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A choice is a decision to pick one thing or action from several. When you choose, you pick the one you want. «I have made my choice» means the person has decided which one to pick.
explain: Choice can also mean the chance or right to choose, as in «You have a choice». It can also mean the range of things you can pick from, as in «a big choice of books». Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Some hard choices have no good option. A dilemma is a hard choice where every option costs something. «A dilemma is a hard choice where every option costs something» tells you that even the best pick still gives something up.
fact: A choice is a decision to pick one thing from several.
fact: «Make a choice» means decide which one to pick.
fact: «A big choice of books» means many books to pick from.
fact: «Spoilt for choice» means having so many good options that picking one is hard.
fact: Choice can also be an adjective: «choice» means high quality or rare.
exercise: «I have made my choice.» What does choice mean here? | A broken toy | The chance to pick something later | A list of many things | *The thing you picked
exercise: In a «multiple choice» test, what do you do? | Ask the teacher to choose for you | Write a long story about the topic | Draw a picture of each answer | *Pick the right answer from several
exercise: What does «spoilt for choice» mean? | Being very tired and hungry | Having no options at all | *Having so many good options that picking one is hard | Being rude to your friends
test: «Clubs are for fun and learning, so the best choice depends on what the child enjoys.» What should decide the best club? | The price only | What other families do | The closest building | *What the child enjoys
test: «In safety, the safe choice is the one to pick when unsure.» Which choice is the safe one when you are unsure? | The one that is most exciting | *The one that keeps you safe | The one that takes the longest | The one your friend picks
exam: «A dilemma is a hard choice where every option costs something.» What is a dilemma? | A choice that is easy and free | A type of medicine | *A hard choice where every option costs something | A lifeboat with room for everyone
